# BLoC Authoring Rules

All business logic is implemented as `@RxBloc()` classes generated via **`rx_bloc_generator`** and composed with **`rxdart`**. These conventions are enforced by every existing BLoC in the codebase and MUST be followed for new ones.

## 1. File Layout

- One bloc per file: `<name>_bloc.dart` next to any sibling in `blocs/` folder.
- Generated code goes into `<name>_bloc.rxb.g.dart` via `part`. Complex private helpers (multi-field validation, DTO mapping) go into `<name>_bloc_extensions.dart`, also via `part`.
- Always declare the `part` directives **before** the contract classes.

```dart
part 'login_bloc.rxb.g.dart';
part 'login_bloc_extensions.dart'; // optional, only if it exists
```

## 2. Three-Class Skeleton

Every bloc exposes exactly three top-level declarations in this order:

1. `abstract class <Name>BlocEvents` — one `void` method per user-initiated action.
2. `abstract class <Name>BlocStates` — one getter per observable state, typed as `Stream<T>` or `ConnectableStream<T>`.
3. `@RxBloc() class <Name>Bloc extends $<Name>Bloc` — the implementation.

Doc-comment each event/state. The `$<Name>Bloc` base class is generated — never write it by hand.

```dart
abstract class DashboardBlocEvents {
  void fetchData();
}

abstract class DashboardBlocStates {
  Stream<bool> get isLoading;
  Stream<ErrorModel> get errors;
  Stream<Result<String>> get data;
}

@RxBloc()
class DashboardBloc extends $DashboardBloc {
  DashboardBloc(this._service);

  final DashboardService _service;

  @override
  Stream<Result<String>> _mapToDataState() => _$fetchDataEvent
      .startWith(null)
      .switchMap((_) => _service.fetchData().asResultStream())
      .setResultStateHandler(this)
      .shareReplay(maxSize: 1);

  @override
  Stream<bool> _mapToIsLoadingState() => loadingState;

  @override
  Stream<ErrorModel> _mapToErrorsState() => errorState.mapToErrorModel();
}
```

## 3. Events

- Fire-and-forget methods returning `void`. Parameters are the payload.
- Use `@RxBlocEvent(type: RxBlocEventType.behaviour, seed: <value>)` for inputs that must replay their latest value (text fields, filters, pagination reset flags). Default (`publish`) is fine for one-shot actions like `login()` or `loadPage()`.
- Inside the bloc, subscribe to the generated `_$<eventName>Event` stream; never invoke the public method from within the class except to trigger a self-dispatch.

```dart
@RxBlocEvent(type: RxBlocEventType.behaviour, seed: '')
void setEmail(String email);

void login();
```

## 4. States

- Standard triplet present on nearly every bloc: `Stream<bool> isLoading`, `Stream<ErrorModel> errors`, plus feature-specific streams.
- Wire `isLoading`/`errors` via the generated handlers — do not reinvent them:

```dart
@override
Stream<bool> _mapToIsLoadingState() => loadingState;

@override
Stream<ErrorModel> _mapToErrorsState() => errorState.mapToErrorModel();
```

- If different async actions need distinct loading scopes, switch the state to `Stream<LoadingWithTag>` and return `loadingWithTagState`; tag each `asResultStream(tag: ...)`:

```dart
abstract class CounterBlocStates {
  Stream<LoadingWithTag> get isLoading;
  // ...
}

@RxBloc()
class CounterBloc extends $CounterBloc {
  static const tagIncrement = 'Increment';
  static const tagDecrement = 'Decrement';

  @override
  Stream<LoadingWithTag> _mapToIsLoadingState() => loadingWithTagState;

  @override
  Stream<int> _mapToCountState() => Rx.merge<Result<Count>>([
        _$incrementEvent.switchMap(
          (_) => _service.increment().asResultStream(tag: tagIncrement),
        ),
        _$decrementEvent.switchMap(
          (_) => _service.decrement().asResultStream(tag: tagDecrement),
        ),
      ])
      .setResultStateHandler(this)
      .whereSuccess()
      .map((e) => e.value)
      .shareReplay(maxSize: 1);
}
```

- Use `@RxBlocIgnoreState()` on getters that only proxy an event stream or a `BehaviorSubject`; do not implement them via `_mapTo...State`.
- State streams that must survive rebuilds end with `.shareReplay(maxSize: 1)`. Use `ConnectableStream<T>` + `.publish()` / `.publishReplay(maxSize: 1)` when the stream must be active **before** any UI subscribes (routing, login success, one-shot effects). Call `xxx.connect().addTo(_compositeSubscription)` from the constructor.

```dart
@RxBloc()
class LoginBloc extends $LoginBloc {
  LoginBloc(this._service, this._router) {
    loggedIn.connect().addTo(_compositeSubscription);
    onRouting.connect().addTo(_compositeSubscription);
  }

  @override
  ConnectableStream<bool> _mapToLoggedInState() => _$loginEvent
      .exhaustMap((_) => _service.login().asResultStream())
      .setResultStateHandler(this)
      .whereSuccess()
      .doOnData((_) => _router.go(const DashboardRoute().routeLocation))
      .startWith(false)
      .publish();
}
```

## 5. Dependency Injection

- Inject **services** (not repositories, not data sources) via the constructor; keep fields `final` and private.
- For cross-bloc signalling, inject a shared coordinator type (e.g. `CoordinatorBlocType`) instead of another feature bloc.
- For navigation, inject `GoRouter` and route via typed routes: `_router.go(const DashboardRoute().routeLocation)`.

## 6. Stream Composition Guide

| Situation | Operator |
|---|---|
| New input supersedes the in-flight request | `switchMap` |
| Ignore taps while a request is in flight (login, register) | `exhaustMap` / `throttleTime(...)` |
| Combine latest values of multiple streams on an event | `withLatestFrom` / `withLatestFromN` |
| Merge heterogeneous triggers into one pipeline | `Rx.merge([...])` with a small private sealed signal type |
| Text search debouncing | `.debounceTime(...)` + `.distinct()` before the network call |

Always finish an async pipeline with `.asResultStream()` → `.setResultStateHandler(this)`; use `.whereSuccess()` / `.whereError()` afterwards. This is what plugs the pipeline into `loadingState` and `errorState` automatically.

## 7. Subscriptions & Disposal

- Every subscription / `connect()` MUST be piped through `.addTo(_compositeSubscription)` — the base class disposes it.
- If the bloc owns `BehaviorSubject`s, override `dispose()` to close them, then call `super.dispose()` at the end.

```dart
final _paginatedListSubject =
    BehaviorSubject<PaginatedList<Item>>.seeded(
      PaginatedList(list: [], pageSize: _pageSize),
    );

@override
void dispose() {
  _paginatedListSubject.close();
  super.dispose();
}
```

## 8. Pagination (`rx_bloc_list`)

When a state is a `Stream<PaginatedList<T>>`:

- Back it with `final _paginated = BehaviorSubject<PaginatedList<T>>.seeded(PaginatedList(list: [], pageSize: _pageSize));`.
- Expose `void loadPage({bool reset = false})` (or equivalent) as the sole event; on `reset: true` call `_paginated.value.reset()` before fetching.
- Use `pageToLoad` (or `pageNumber + 1`) as the page argument, `.switchMap` into the service, then `.setResultStateHandler(this).mergeWithPaginatedList(_paginated).bind(_paginated)` and return `_paginated` from `_mapTo...State`.

```dart
@override
Stream<PaginatedList<Item>> _mapToItemsState() => _$loadPageEvent
    .startWith(false)
    .switchMap((reset) {
      if (reset) _paginated.value.reset();
      return _service
          .getItems(
            page: _paginated.value.pageNumber + 1,
            pageSize: _pageSize,
          )
          .asResultStream();
    })
    .setResultStateHandler(this)
    .mergeWithPaginatedList(_paginated)
    .bind(_paginated);
```

For **debounced-search + pagination in one pipeline**, `Rx.merge` the two triggers into a private sealed signal type, `switchMap` once, and reset the paginated list when a query arrives:

```dart
/// Discriminated union describing what triggered the next fetch.
class _FetchTrigger {
  const _FetchTrigger._(this.filter, this.resetRequested);
  factory _FetchTrigger.filter(String value) => _FetchTrigger._(value, false);
  factory _FetchTrigger.page(bool reset) => _FetchTrigger._(null, reset);

  final String? filter;
  final bool resetRequested;
  bool get isFilter => filter != null;
}

// ...

ProductsBloc(this._service) {
  final debouncedFilter = _$onFilterChangedEvent
      .map((v) => v.trim())
      .debounceTime(const Duration(milliseconds: 300))
      .distinct()
      .map(_FetchTrigger.filter);

  final paging = _$loadPageEvent.map(_FetchTrigger.page);

  Rx.merge<_FetchTrigger>([debouncedFilter, paging])
      .switchMap((trigger) {
        // A new filter (or explicit refresh) always restarts pagination.
        if (trigger.isFilter || trigger.resetRequested) {
          _paginated.value.reset();
        }
        final filter = trigger.isFilter ? trigger.filter! : _currentFilter;
        _currentFilter = filter;

        return _service
            .fetchProducts(
              filter: filter,
              page: _paginated.value.pageNumber + 1,
              pageSize: _pageSize,
            )
            .asResultStream();
      })
      .setResultStateHandler(this)
      .mergeWithPaginatedList(_paginated)
      .bind(_paginated)
      .addTo(_compositeSubscription);
}
```

## 9. Things to Avoid

- Don't hand-roll `StreamController` when a generated event or `BehaviorSubject` fits.
- Don't call repositories / data sources / Dio from a bloc — always go through a service.
- Don't put UI concerns (`BuildContext`, widgets, `SnackBar`s) inside a bloc. Emit a state; let the page react via `RxBlocListener` / `RxBlocBuilder`.
- Don't mix `async`/`await` with reactive pipelines inside `_mapTo...State`; stick to `rxdart` operators so error/loading handlers wire up correctly.
- Don't emit from another bloc directly — route it through a shared coordinator bloc.

## Archetype Cheatsheet

| Archetype | Shape |
|---|---|
| Minimal single-state | one event, one `_mapTo...State` using `switchMap` + `asResultStream` + `shareReplay(maxSize: 1)`. |
| Tagged loading | `Stream<LoadingWithTag>` state + multiple `Rx.merge`-ed events with `asResultStream(tag: ...)`. |
| Form + routing | `@RxBlocEvent(behaviour, seed: '')` input events, `ConnectableStream` result + routing streams connected in constructor, `withLatestFrom` to pick up current field values on submit. |
| Paginated list | `BehaviorSubject<PaginatedList<T>>` + `loadPage({bool reset = false})` + `mergeWithPaginatedList` + `bind`. |
| Debounced search + pagination | `Rx.merge` debounced query stream with page stream into a sealed signal; single `switchMap`. |
| Global event hub / coordinator | no state mapping; expose events as `@RxBlocIgnoreState()` streams so other blocs can subscribe. |
